From: =?UTF-8?q?Ho=C3=A0n=20Tr=E1=BA=A7n?= <hoantn801@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 17:58:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Notification Center: global shell loader + badge redesign

Make the Notification Center work on EVERY custom eCentric Workspace page
(not just the homepage) and polish the unread badge.

Root cause: the NC asset was injected only into the homepage Web Page record
(patch p001, anchored on the Action Center widget). Other shell pages never
received the loader, so their legacy bell handler still showed
"feature in development".

Fix (single shared loader point, no per-page work):
* hooks.py: register the asset via web_include_js so Frappe injects it on every
  website-rendered page exactly once. Deliberately NOT app_include_js (that would
  load on Frappe Desk /app and bind its native bell).
* notification_center.js:
  - precise Frappe Desk guard (/app or /app/...), never lookalikes like /approval
  - adopt the native bell via clone+replace -> strips any legacy click handler,
    keeps href so Ctrl/Cmd/middle-click still open /app/notification-log
  - plain left-click also stopPropagation -> defeats document-level legacy toast
  - badge redesign: 1-9 = ~16px circle, 9+ = ~21px pill, 9-10px semibold,
    2px white ring, existing --pink token, anchored top-right (absolute, no
    header shift), fully hidden at 0
  - idempotent badge mount + dropdown build; single-install guard unchanged
    (homepage still carries the legacy <script>; second load is a no-op)

Backend, permissions, Weekly Report and Alert Center logic are untouched.

Tests: 36 existing pass + 15 new (TestGlobalShellLoader, TestDomRuntime).
A node DOM-runtime harness exercises the real asset to prove badge 0/1/9/10+,
single badge/dropdown, reinstall-no-duplicate, Desk guard and legacy-handler
stripping.
