Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Notification Center: retire homepage loader + prove
 handler neutralization

Addresses the three review points on the global-shell change.

1. Retire the homepage-only loader (no double-load):
   * NEW cleanup patch p002_retire_homepage_bell_loader removes the
     <script id="ec-notification-center">...</script><!-- /ec-notification-center -->
     block that p001 injected into the homepage Web Page record. Idempotent,
     Action-Center-safe (anchor count preserved), fail-safe. Registered AFTER p001.
   * Requires a ONE-TIME 'bench migrate' on deploy. After migrate, /home -- like
     every other page -- loads the asset exactly once (the install guard is now
     only defence-in-depth, not the de-dup mechanism).

2. Legacy 'feature in development' handler neutralization, proven (not string-only):
   * adoptBell() clone+replace drops addEventListener listeners AND the onclick
     property handler; removeAttribute('onclick') drops the inline attribute.
   * stopPropagation/stopImmediatePropagation now run on EVERY bell click so a
     document-level delegated legacy handler can never fire; native nav is kept for
     modifier/middle-click (we never preventDefault there).
   * NEW bell_click_check.js executes the real asset against a bubbling mini-DOM and
     proves, per route (/home, /overview, /approval): plain left-click opens the
     dropdown + fires NO legacy handler (inline/property/addEventListener/delegated)
     + cancels native nav; Ctrl/middle-click keep native nav and open nothing; Desk
     /app and a public no-bell page stay inert.

Tests: 55 pass (36 original + 19 new), incl. both node runtime harnesses.
